1. Work performed: removed unconditional hot-path `cudaDeviceSynchronize()` calls from the primitive ops, dense GEMM, NVFP4 GEMM, embedding lookup, device argmax, and FP8 quantize path. In the NVFP4 pack path I also removed the temporary `global_max_bits` alloc/free by reusing the existing tensor-scale buffer, and I changed `DeviceTensorFp32::Create()`, `DeviceTensorBf16::Create()`, and `DeviceNvfp4Matrix::Create()` to use a one-time static CUDA availability check instead of per-allocation `cudaGetDeviceCount()`. I kept launch-error checks, left D2H synchronization behavior intact via blocking `cudaMemcpy(..., cudaMemcpyDeviceToHost)`, and did not touch env-gated debug/compare paths. `expert_layer.cpp` did not need a code change here because the dead fallback allocations called out in the review are already after the direct/fused early return in the current tree.

2. Compile status: both requested builds passed.
`cmake --build build-phase1-tests --target nemotron_runtime_backend -j4`
`cmake --build build-phase1-tests --target full_forward_manifest_smoke_test -j4`

3. Concerns about correctness: the default-stream ordering assumption matches the current implementation, so removing these explicit syncs should preserve device-to-device correctness. The remaining risk is performance-related, not semantic: several paths still do per-token `cudaMalloc/cudaFree`, and `cudaFree` is still an implicit barrier until step 8b. I verified builds only in this checkpoint; I did not run the smoke binary or re-profile decode yet.

